sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Py as User Python
    participant Brg as spike_bridge.py
    participant Wkr as Worker bridge
    participant Main as main.js
    participant Sim as RobotSimulator<br/>(simulator.js)
    participant W2D as World2D<br/>(world_2d.js)
    participant B2D as Box2D-WASM
    participant Cnv as Canvas
    participant Blk as Blockly generated JS

    rect rgb(238, 246, 255)
    Note over Py,Cnv: A · Per-step raycast during a motion command
    Py->>Brg: motor_pair.move(...)
    Brg->>Wkr: bridgeSend({type:'move', ...})
    Wkr->>Main: postMessage
    Main->>Sim: executeCommand(cmd)
    loop each physics step (~16 ms)
        Sim->>W2D: setKinematicVelocity / step(dt)
        W2D->>B2D: world.Step(sub, 8, 3)
        Sim->>Sim: _updateDistanceSensor()
        Sim->>W2D: castRay(origin, heading, 2000, {excludeBody: robotBody})
        W2D->>B2D: world.RayCast(cb, p1, p2)
        B2D-->>W2D: ReportFixture(fixture, point, normal, frac)
        Note right of W2D: skip if fixture.GetBody().a == robotBody.a
        W2D-->>Sim: {hit, distanceMm, point, normal}
        Sim->>Sim: robot.sensors.distanceMM/Hit/Origin
        Sim->>Cnv: _draw → _drawDistanceSensorRay (line + label)
    end
    Sim-->>Main: _sensorState() = {distance_mm, ...}
    Main-->>Wkr: postMessage(sensor snapshot)
    Wkr->>Brg: _state.update(...)
    Brg-->>Py: (motion call returns)
    end

    rect rgb(248, 244, 236)
    Note over Py,Brg: B · Python sensor read (cached path)
    Py->>Brg: distance_sensor.distance(F)
    Brg->>Brg: v = _state['distance_mm']
    Brg-->>Py: v < 9999 ? v : -1
    end

    rect rgb(244, 248, 240)
    Note over Blk,Sim: C · Blockly sensor read (direct, on-demand recompute)
    Blk->>Sim: getDistanceSensorValue()
    Sim->>Sim: _updateDistanceSensor()
    Sim->>W2D: castRay(...)
    W2D->>B2D: world.RayCast(...)
    B2D-->>W2D: ReportFixture(...)
    W2D-->>Sim: {hit, distanceMm, ...}
    Sim-->>Blk: distanceMM (mm)
    end
